        "original_id": "59d04a98-7f89-53a3-9795-fd9c2d0bcf78",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Walkley Heights, South Australia; Yatala Labour Prison\n- People: R. M. Williams; Sir Thomas Playford\n- Organizations: Yatala Labour Prison\n- Concepts: prison farm; compulsory acquisition; quarrying rock\n\nFacts:\n- Yatala Labour Prison was built in 1854 to enable prisoners to work at the creek quarrying rock for roads and construction.\n- Walkley Heights, South Australia, is located on land that formerly comprised the prison farm for Yatala Labour Prison.\n- Walkley Heights, South Australia, includes fifty-five hectares of land formerly owned by R. M. Williams.\n- The South Australian government compulsorily acquired the fifty-five hectares formerly owned by R. M. Williams during the time of former State Premier Sir Thomas Playford.",
